<section>
  <p class="section-date">1854</p>

  <h2>The Cholera Epidemic in Naples, Italy</h2>

  <div class="rubini-intro-layout">

    <div class="rubini-intro-text">

      <p>
        Some of the most remarkable documents I encountered during this
        research came from Naples.
      </p>

      <p>
        During the 1854 cholera epidemic, Dr. Rocco Rubini was appointed to
        direct treatment among the male population of the{" "}
        <em>Reale Albergo de' Poveri</em>, a large charitable institution
        in Naples.
      </p>

      <p>
        Rubini later published institutional correspondence, official
        certificates and patient registers relating to his work.
      </p>

      <p>
        A certificate dated September 11, 1854 recorded a male population
        of 1,268 at the institution.
      </p>

      <p>
        From July 27 through September 11, it stated that:
      </p>

    </div>

    <div class="stat-card rubini-stat-card">
      <p class="stat-number">200</p>
      <p class="stat-label">men were attacked by cholera</p>

      <div class="stat-divider"></div>

      <p class="stat-number secondary">All reportedly recovered</p>
    </div>

  </div>


  <!-- SEPTEMBER 11 CERTIFICATE: IMAGE LEFT / TEXT RIGHT -->

  <div class="document-layout figure-left rubini-document-layout">

    <figure class="historical-document">
      <img
        src="/images/history/rubini-certificate-september-11-1854.jpg"
